{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"The main testing complication is `compare_allocations`: sequential C-then-Rust calls perturb the shared allocator’s free-list order, which can create a false mismatch in its pointer-order branch. The tests will insert one neutral C allocation call between paired composed calls so both libraries observe the same allocator orientation, while all functions remain invoked through symbols loaded from each `.so`. I’m now adding `libloading` and the deterministic randomized test harness."}}
